hree items, the first MAJOR. VERIFIED CORRECT FIRST: all three algebraic clauses hold as stated over a commutative ring with involution — 1 is sigma-unitary since sigma(1)*1 = 1; closure follows from sigma(uv)uv = sigma(u)u * sigma(v)v = 1 by commutativity; rigidity is immediate (sigma(u) = u and sigma(u)u = 1 give u^2 = 1); and clause 3 is its contrapositive. The unimodularity |Phi_b(z)| = 1 for real z and real b is also correct — it is the standard consequence of the Faddeev unitarity relation. (1) FALSE IMPLICATION, and it is load-bearing. The Interpretation opens: 'On the fibre saddle — real b, so q = e^{2 pi i b^2} is a root of unity —'. Real b does NOT make q a root of unity: e^{2 pi i theta} is a root of unity if and only if theta is RATIONAL, so q is a root of unity exactly when b^2 is rational, and for generic real b it is an irrational point on the unit circle. What real b does give is |q| = 1, which is all the unimodularity argument actually needs. The error matters because 'the root-of-unity (Faddeev) saddle' is the phrase this block and its sibling rem:phi-b-bar-parity-interpretation use to separate the two archimedean faces, and the block's own evidence list is precisely the RATIONAL cases (zeta_4, zeta_5^2, zeta_6, self-dual), i.e. special b^2, not general real b. Proposed: 'real b, so |q| = 1 (and q is a root of unity exactly when b^2 is rational)'. (2) THE MANIFEST CONTRADICTS THE PROSE. The .md says the unimodularity is 'witnessed on the validated evaluator at the zeta_4, zeta_5^2, zeta_6 and self-dual points', but the .ts computation block records status: 'not_run' and carries NO witness field, while naming computations/qbeta/qbeta_fmap_phi_b_root_of_unity_reference.py (which does exist on disk, 6505 bytes). So a computational confirmation is asserted in prose that the manifest says was never run. Proposed: run the reference script and attach a witness, or downgrade 'witnessed' to 'expected'. (3) MINOR: 'analytically this is the reflection w -> -bar w of the Faddeev contour integral' is offered as the analytic ground for clause-2's hypothesis but is neither derived nor cited.","history":2},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-21","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:v03","history":2},{"id":"uses-editorial-hygiene","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-09-03","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"uses-formal-coverage","group":"uses","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-09-03","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-uses.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-09-03","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-09","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-voice.ts","history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"voice","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":